cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use LunarLab in your research, please cite the software using the
  metadata in this file (version and, once a release is archived, its DOI).
type: software
title: LunarLab
abstract: >-
  LunarLab is a local-first platform for auditing reward design in
  reinforcement learning on Gymnasium's LunarLander-v3 with Stable-Baselines3
  PPO and DQN. It records the original and the shaped (training) reward
  separately for every transition, implements potential-based reward shaping
  and a deliberately flawed hover bonus, detects reward exploitation, freezes
  validation-selected checkpoints before a disjoint final test, reports
  statistics across training seeds, and supports robustness, learned-reward
  (preference) and hyperparameter-tuning studies, with a command-line
  interface, a Python API and a local web interface.
